# Database Configuration
# Replace with your actual PostgreSQL connection string
# Format: postgresql://username:password@host:port/database_name
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://localhost:5432/kutuma

# Environment
NODE_ENV=development

# API Configuration
# For development with Rork backend (auto-configured)
EXPO_PUBLIC_RORK_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8787

# Optional: Email Service (for production)
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=your-email@gmail.com
# SMTP_PASSWORD=your-app-password

# Optional: SMS Service (for production OTP)
# AFRICAS_TALKING_API_KEY=your-api-key
# AFRICAS_TALKING_USERNAME=your-username

# ============================================
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS
# ============================================

# 1. Copy this file to .env:
#    cp .env.example .env

# 2. Update DATABASE_URL with your PostgreSQL credentials

# 3. Set up the database:
#    a. Option 1 - Local PostgreSQL:
#       - Install PostgreSQL: https://www.postgresql.org/download/
#       - Create database: createdb kutuma
#       - Update DATABASE_URL accordingly
#
#    b. Option 2 - Supabase (Recommended):
#       - Sign up at https://supabase.com
#       - Create a new project
#       - Get connection string from Settings > Database
#       - Use the "Connection string" (not "Connection pooling")
#
#    c. Option 3 - Neon:
#       - Sign up at https://neon.tech
#       - Create a new project
#       - Copy the connection string

# 4. Run database migrations:
#    bunx drizzle-kit generate
#    bunx drizzle-kit push

# 5. (Optional) Seed the database with sample data:
#    bun backend/db/seed.ts

# ============================================
# CURRENT STATUS
# ============================================
# The app is designed to work WITHOUT a database for development
# If database is not available:
# - Users are stored in-memory only
# - Sessions are temporary
# - OTP codes are logged to console
# - You can still test the full auth flow

# For production, you MUST set up the database properly.
